A main-thread command that runs the append to the top-level .gitignore of the sandbox repo through a nested bash -c invocation, followed by a second command (ls x), must be DENIED. The nested shell hides the write from the outer command scan, so the guard must look inside the bash -c string. This pins the deny that the nested-scan fix in 9db8a72 now gives, so the case is expected to PASS on this commit.
